# Aamantran website — public environment.
#
# This codebase is deployed TWICE from the same branch, differing only by the
# values below. Everything NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the browser bundle at
# `next build`, so changing any of these needs a rebuild, not a restart.
#
#   aamantran.online      -> the India storefront: rupees, GST added at checkout
#   aamantranglobal.com   -> the international storefront: dollars, zero-rated
#
# ── Storefront ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 'IN' or 'INTL'. Anything else (including unset) is treated as 'IN', which is
# the safe default: it charges GST and quotes the lower price, so a missing
# value can never overcharge someone or skip tax that was owed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STOREFRONT=IN
# Global deployment: NEXT_PUBLIC_STOREFRONT=INTL

# ── This deployment's own origin ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Feeds metadataBase, every canonical, the sitemap and all JSON-LD. MUST differ
# between the two deployments — if the global build canonicalises itself to
# aamantran.online, Google will not index it as a separate site.
# Use the www form, matching the apex -> www redirect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.aamantran.online
# Global deployment: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.aamantranglobal.com

# ── Backend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One API serves both storefronts, so this is the SAME on both deployments.
# Defaults to https://api.aamantran.online in production, localhost:4000 in dev.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.aamantran.online

# Couple dashboard. Also shared.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COUPLE_DASHBOARD_URL=https://app.aamantran.online

# Public media bucket (template thumbnails, review photos). Shared.
# Read at build time by next.config.ts to allow image optimisation for this host.
# Defaults to https://media.aamantran.online when unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_URL=https://media.aamantran.online

# ── Tracking ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One pixel per site — mixing both storefronts into a single dataset would blend
# rupee and dollar conversion values into meaningless ad metrics.
#
# The code already picks the right one from NEXT_PUBLIC_STOREFRONT:
#   IN   -> 1106272148422147   (aamantran.online)
#   INTL -> 1403963484478935   (aamantranglobal.com)
# so this only needs setting to override one of those, e.g. when an ad account
# moves. LEAVE IT UNSET on the global deployment unless it holds the global id —
# whatever is here wins, and India's pixel set here would swallow every dollar
# conversion.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# Social handles. Shared by both deployments — the same brand accounts.
# The code fallbacks are correct, so these are belt-and-braces rather than
# required; set them anyway so each service states its own configuration.
# The Instagram value also becomes the Organization JSON-LD `sameAs`, i.e. the
# account search engines treat as official.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_HANDLE=aamantran_online
# NEXT_PUBLIC_YOUTUBE_HANDLE=aamantran_online-h2t

# ── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Skips the real PayU redirect and settles the order through /mock-success.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DUMMY_PAYMENT_MODE=true
